  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing Acute Malnutrition through Agriculture and Nutrition-sensitive Interventions in Borno and Yobe States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide nutrition and food security assistance to vulnerable communities affected by malnutrition in north-east Nigeria. This FAO project produces nutrient dense local food, and provides food vouchers and vegetable seeds, among other activities. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 11,500 people in the Nutrition sector, including 3,000 women, 7,000 children, and 550 persons with disabilities, and 21,000 people in the Food Security sector, including 10,500 women and 275 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
